  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nDespite southward movement of an upper level trough through\nTuesday, limited moisture and convergence means the region sees\nminimal changes to the prevailing dry and seasonable pattern\nthrough Wednesday.\n\nThe central CONUS ridge slides east to end the week, resulting\nin temperature rising to more summer-like levels but offering\nlimited risks for heat impacts outside of urban centers due to\ndelays in rising humidity levels. \n\nLong-range ensemble vary in the timing and degree of the likely\nbreakdown of said bridge over the weekend into early next week\n(meaning current day 6/7 PoPs may vary notable for ensuing\nforecast cycles). Regardless, such occurrence favors the \nreintroduction of shower and thunderstorm chances with some\nmodicum of severe risks pending the finer details of the\nsynoptic pattern and environmental conditions.",
